## Architectural Notes

- The service-worker stale constants are already close to the target shape from
  the top-level rethink: opening, ready, action, and close deadlines. The next
  step is to attach them to explicit job attempts and leases rather than
  metadata plus progress heartbeat.
- The foreground-promotion waits and `maxReverseAttempts = 3` are the main
  tactical layer. They made the 8-profile repeatability case work, but they
  should not be expanded.
- Performance work should not start by shrinking these values. The current
  slow batch time is more likely from foreground contention than from any one
  large timeout.
- The next scheduler slice should make one tab own the interactive foreground
  lease while other tabs preload or wait. After that, these timeout values can
  be retuned with cleaner evidence.
